  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "notes": "Boot an Avengers ROM from an empty NVRAM and enter the S.A.M. switch test with the named Back and Select service keys (Back, then Select five times: service-menu splash, icon menu, diagnostics menu, switch menu, switch test). The scenario names no game, so one byte-identical file serves the Limited Edition avs_170h and the Pro avs_170. Hold each public switch for 3 s with a snapshot while held and another 2 s after release: 47 (left orbit, a control), 58, 61, 58 and 61 again, and 48 (right ramp exit, a second control). The switch test prints the ROM's own name and wire colours for the switch it reads closed, and NONE once it is released. S.A.M. applies no inversion, so a held public 1 is a closed contact. The held addresses lie in the playfield matrix, outside every cabinet input the named keys drive.",
